ta-tip=\"Forecast said 41%&amp;#10;It rained 38% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 77 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"202.17454545454547\" cy=\"244.9090909090909\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 75%&amp;#10;It rained 55% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 69 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"323.0382608695652\" cy=\"181.53623188405797\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 97%&amp;#10;It rained 79% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 86 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"399.9393023255815\" cy=\"94.18604651162792\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(22%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Constanta the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>winter</b> (0.36) and least in\n<b>summer</b> (0.23).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>184</td><td class='num'>9%</td><td class='num'>0.234</td><td class='num'>1.3%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>217</td><td class='num'>24%</td><td class='num'>0.300</td><td class='num'>7.1%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>29%</td><td class='num'>0.308</td><td class='num'>10.8%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>27%</td><td class='num'>0.357</td><td class='num'>9.7%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":44.18073,"lon":28.63432,"n":761,"n_cities":216,"name":"Constanta","offset_days":-1,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.03,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.0,"n":348,"obs":0.031609195402298854,"sig":true},{"hi":0.1,"lo":0.03,"mean":0.046111111111111124,"n":108,"obs":0.1111111111111111,"sig":true},{"hi":0.25,"lo":0.1,"mean":0.1523287671232877,"n":73,"obs":0.1643835616438356,"sig":false},{"hi":0.6,"lo":0.25,"mean":0.4072727272727273,"n":77,"obs":0.37662337662337664,"sig":false},{"hi":0.9,"lo":0.6,"mean":0.748695652173913,"n":69,"obs":0.5507246376811594,"sig":true},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.9,"mean":0.9659302325581398,"n":86,"obs":0.7906976744186046,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":4.4,"provisional":false,"rank":82,"rank_hi":144.0,"rank_lo":41.0,"reliability":0.008189199139644745,"resolution":0.06740387164908514,"skill_pct":null,"slug":"constanta","station":"CONSTANTA","timezone":"Europe/Bucharest"}